    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17930" root="زكم" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَزْكُومٌ</span></b>  [pass. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَمَ</span>]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِرْبَةٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَزْكُومَةٌ</span> <i>A filled water-skin.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And,
applied to a man, (AZ, As, S,) <i>Affected with</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُكَام</span>: (AZ, As, S, Msb, K:) [regularly formed
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَمَهُ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُكِمَ</span>; but thought to be] from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَزْكَمَهُ</span>; (AZ, As, S, Msb;) [and therefore] anomalous. (Msb.)

